{"title":"Modular inverse","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">modular arithmetic</a>, given a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6beb32d67786a727a35fb8b54093c4b6d2bd404a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\in \\{1,2,3,\\ldots,m-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" /> is the modular inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0634e1ad41bae775b0c67ddfd87efa15c700cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy \\equiv 1 \\pmod{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />. The inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is commonly denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158ff9beaae8886323fb0e77e0fc77484b2a0dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{-1}$\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" />, and exists if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba38b2f9142fa443015e2808872120285537756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{-1}=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />, then we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfacd03fd6105d4b39c1872809e346fee2e3d83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{-1}=x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This is equivalent to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiplicative_inverse\" title=\"Multiplicative inverse\">multiplicative inverse</a>. \n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_inverse&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100617\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1919/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.241      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.241      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21780:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018100617 and revision id 283090. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}